Q: How do I make it so that the script responds differently for each element? A: <p>Avoid using the <code>id</code> attribute when programming such logic. Use the <code>class</code>
attribute and write JavaScript code which will loop over all of the items
and then bind the click handlers for the behaviors. This way, you don't need
to hard-code the ids at several places.</p>
<p>But, <strong>you don't need any JavaScript to do this as in 2026</strong>, you can use the
<code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> tag and bind the buttons. This is an
<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79989158/653182">example I made on another Stackoverflow question</a>:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>:root {
  --dialog-padding: 1rem;
  --dialog-bg-color: white; /* Try replacing it with the debugger. */
  --dialog-backdrop-bg-color: rgb(0 0 0 / 5%);
  --dialog-box-shadow: 0 0 1em rgb(0 0 0 / 30%);
  --dialog-banner-bg-color: #00bcd4; /* Turquoise. */
  --dialog-content-stripe-color: rgb(0 0 0 / 10%);
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

/* Common styling for dialogs. */
dialog {
  padding: 0; /* Will be set on the child .dialog-content element. */
  background-color: var(--dialog-bg-color);
  border: 2px solid var(--dialog-banner-bg-color);
  box-shadow: var(--dialog-box-shadow);
}

dialog::backdrop {
  background: var(--dialog-backdrop-bg-color);
}

/* Blur and desaturate all other elements when the dialog is open. */
body:has(dialog[open]) &gt; *:not(dialog) {
  filter: blur(1px) grayscale(.7);
}

.dialog-banner {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  background-color: var(--dialog-banner-bg-color);
  /* Automatically switch black/white text color. */
  color: contrast-color(var(--dialog-banner-bg-color));
  /* Set same border width as the dialog padding. */
  border: var(--dialog-padding) solid var(--dialog-bg-color);
  /* But not below the dialog banner. */
  border-bottom: none;
}

/* Instead of a box-shadow, let's create a gradient to slowly
   hide the text which will scroll up beneath it. */
.dialog-banner::after {
  content: "";
  display: block;
  background: linear-gradient(0deg, transparent 0%, var(--dialog-bg-color) 100%);
  position: absolute;
  /* Put it at the bottom of the banner. */
  top: 100%;
  /* Make it bigger, to fill all the dialog width. */
  left: calc(-1 * var(--dialog-padding));
  width: calc(100% + 2 * var(--dialog-padding));
  height: 1.5em; /* Can be adjusted, but not too high. */
}

.dialog-content {
  padding: var(--dialog-padding);
}

.dialog-content &gt; *:first-child {
  margin-top: 0;
}

.dialog-content &gt; *:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

/* Dialog menu. */
.dialog-menu ul {
  display: flex;
  list-style-type: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.dialog-menu li {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.dialog-menu a {
  &amp;:link, &amp;:visited {
    text-decoration: none;
    display: block;
    color: inherit;
    padding: .25em .5em;
  }
  &amp;:hover, &amp;:active {
    /* Lighter background color on hover. */
    background-color: oklch(
      from var(--dialog-banner-bg-color)
      calc(l + .05) c h
    );
  }
  /* Show the first letter (access key) on hover.
     F and E may conflict with browser's access keys. */
  &amp;:hover::first-letter {
    border-bottom: 1px dotted;
  }
}

/* Specific styling for Dialog 1. */
#dialog-1 {
  width: 240px;
}
#dialog-1 .dialog-content {
  font-size: 32px;
  /* Let's put a background, to show that the banner bottom
     shadow/gradient is filling the full width of the dialog. */
  background-image: linear-gradient(
    0deg,
    transparent 0%,
    transparent 80%,
    var(--dialog-content-stripe-color) 80%,
    var(--dialog-content-stripe-color) 100%
  );
  background-size: 10px 10px;
}

/* Specific styling for Dialog 2. */
#dialog-2 {
  --dialog-bg-color: #fdffe5;
  --dialog-banner-bg-color: #ddc482;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="buttons"&gt;
  &lt;button commandfor="dialog-1" command="show-modal"&gt;Dialog 1&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button commandfor="dialog-2" command="show-modal"&gt;Dialog 2&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;dialog id="dialog-1" closedby="any"&gt;
  &lt;div class="dialog-banner"&gt;
    &lt;nav class="dialog-menu"&gt;
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#file" accesskey="f"&gt;File&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#edit" accesskey="e"&gt;Edit&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#tools" accesskey="t"&gt;Tools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#help" accesskey="h"&gt;Help&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/nav&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="dialog-content"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      A long screed which will scroll and scroll and
      scroll but should not scroll behind the banner.
      At least, that's the hope.
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;button command="close" commandfor="dialog-1"&gt;Close&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/dialog&gt;

&lt;dialog id="dialog-2" closedby="any"&gt;
  &lt;div class="dialog-banner"&gt;Dialog 2&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="dialog-content"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      This is just an example of a second dialog
      with some other styling.
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;#dialog-2 {
  --dialog-bg-color: #fdffe5;
  --dialog-banner-bg-color: #ddc482;
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    &lt;button command="close" commandfor="dialog-2"&gt;Close&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/dialog&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lorem_ipsum" target="_blank"&gt;Lorem ipsum&lt;/a&gt; dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Tenetur ab at illum necessitatibus veritatis animi ad vel ullam, numquam repudiandae minus impedit cum? Ullam facilis iste corrupti quis natus eum.&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: Save XML from Url and read it A: <p>Here is code snippet for you ,</p>

<pre><code>  try {

        URL url = new URL("your url goes here");

        //create the new connection
        HttpURLConnection urlConnection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();

        urlConnection.connect();

        //set the path where we want to save the file
        //in this case, going to save it on the root directory of the
        //sd card.
        File SDCardRoot = Environment.getExternalStorageDirectory();
        //create a new file, specifying the path, and the filename
        //which we want to save the file as.
        File file = new File(SDCardRoot,"Demo.xml");

        //this will be used to write the downloaded data into the file we created
        FileOutputStream fileOutput = new FileOutputStream(file);

        //this will be used in reading the data from the internet
        InputStream inputStream = urlConnection.getInputStream();

        //this is the total size of the file
        int totalSize = urlConnection.getContentLength();
        progressDialog.setMax(totalSize);

        //variable to store total downloaded bytes
        int downloadedSize = 0;

        //create a buffer...
        byte[] buffer = new byte[1024];
        int bufferLength = 0; //used to store a temporary size of the buffer

        //now, read through the input buffer and write the contents to the file
        while ( (bufferLength = inputStream.read(buffer)) &gt; 0 ) {
                //add the data in the buffer to the file in the file output stream (the file on the sd card
                fileOutput.write(buffer, 0, bufferLength);
                //add up the size so we know how much is downloaded
                downloadedSize += bufferLength;

        }
        //close the output stream when done
        fileOutput.close();
        //catch some possible errors...
} catch (MalformedURLException e) {
        e.printStackTrace();
} catch (IOException e) {
        e.printStackTrace();
}
</code></pre>

